Pages may be implemented as separate routes, tabs, panels or modals, as long as the required information and permissions remain available.

## Data Fields

### Wishlist Item

A wishlist item represents a specific game that a member wants to obtain.

**Required fields:**

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | identifier | Yes | Unique identifier of the wishlist item |
| `memberId` | member reference | Yes | ID of the member who owns the wishlist item |
| `gameId` | catalogue-game reference | Yes | ID of the desired game |
| `priority` | enum or configured value | Yes | Priority assigned to the desired game |
| `notes` | text | No | Additional information about the desired game |
| `isFulfilled` | boolean | Yes | Indicates whether the wishlist item has been fulfilled |

**Priority values**

The case requires every wishlist item to have a priority but does not define the exact values.

A possible implementation is:

- `LOW`
- `MEDIUM`
- `HIGH`

These values are a proposed implementation choice and must be confirmed with the group or product owner.

**Fulfilled values**

- `false` — the member is still looking for the game.
- `true` — the wishlist item has been fulfilled.

All wishlist items are publicly visible. A separate visibility field is unnecessary because the case does not define private wishlists.

### Trade Offer

A trade offer represents a proposal to exchange one game for another.

**Required fields:**

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `id` | identifier | Yes | Unique identifier of the trade offer |
| `wishlistItemId` | wishlist-item reference | Yes | ID of the wishlist item receiving the offer |
| `offerCreatorId` | member reference | Yes | ID of the member making the offer |
| `requestedGameId` | catalogue-game reference | Yes | ID of the game the offer creator wants in return |
| `createdAt` | date-time | Yes | Date and time when the offer was created |
| `status` | enum | Yes | Current trade offer status |

The game being offered is obtained through the linked wishlist item.

The member receiving the offer is obtained through the owner of that wishlist item.

These relationships prevent unnecessary duplication of data.

### Trade Offer Status Values

- `OPEN`
- `ACCEPTED`
- `REJECTED`
- `CANCELLED`

**Status descriptions**

| Status | Description |
|---|---|
| `OPEN` | The offer has been submitted and is awaiting a decision |
| `ACCEPTED` | The wishlist owner has accepted the offer |
| `REJECTED` | The wishlist owner has rejected the offer |
| `CANCELLED` | The offer creator cancelled the offer, or the system cancelled it because of a conflicting accepted offer |

### Derived Offer Expiration

Expiration is calculated using the offer creation date and the club's configured validity period.

**Calculation:**

`expiresAt = createdAt + configuredValidityPeriod`

`isExpired = currentDateTime > expiresAt`

The exact validity period is not specified in the case and must be configured after agreement with the product owner.

An offer can have status `OPEN` while its validity period has expired.

In that situation, the offer is no longer eligible for acceptance.

### Trade Offer State Transitions

```text
OPEN
 |
 |-- Wishlist owner accepts --> ACCEPTED
 |
 |-- Wishlist owner rejects --> REJECTED
 |
 |-- Offer creator cancels --> CANCELLED
 |
 |-- Conflicting offer accepted --> CANCELLED
```

**Expiration**

```text
OPEN + validity period expired
          |
          v
   Cannot be accepted
```

Expiration does not create an additional stored status.

`ACCEPTED`, `REJECTED` and `CANCELLED` are final offer states.

## Permissions

### Every Signed-in Member

- View their own wishlist.
- View the public wishlists of other members.
- Add games from the catalogue to their own wishlist.
- Assign priorities and notes to their wishlist items.
- View the fulfilled status of wishlist items.
- Submit trade offers for unfulfilled wishlist items belonging to other members.
- View their own sent trade offers.
- Cancel their own open trade offers.
- View the status and expiration of their trade offers.

### Wishlist Owner

- View trade offers received for their wishlist items.
- Accept eligible trade offers for their own wishlist items.
- Reject open trade offers for their own wishlist items.
- View which wishlist items have been fulfilled.
- Cannot accept or reject offers belonging to another member's wishlist.

### Trade Offer Creator

- Create trade offers for other members' unfulfilled wishlist items.
- View the status of their submitted offers.
- Cancel their own offers while they remain open.
- Cannot accept or reject their own submitted offers on behalf of the wishlist owner.
- Cannot manually cancel another member's offer.

### Committee Members

Committee members have the same wishlist and trading permissions as ordinary members.

The case does not grant committee members additional permissions to accept, reject or cancel trade offers belonging to other members.

Permission checks must be enforced by the backend, not only by hiding frontend buttons.

## Business Rules

### Catalogue Relationship

- Every wishlist item must reference an existing game in the shared catalogue.
- The catalogue distinguishes between different editions of the same game.
- Every trade offer must reference an existing wishlist item.
- The game requested in return must also exist in the catalogue.

### Public Visibility

- All wishlists are visible to all members.
- Members can view wishlist items belonging to other members.
- Public visibility does not give members permission to modify another member's wishlist.

### Wishlist Priorities

- Every wishlist item has a priority.
- Priorities indicate the relative importance of desired games.
- The exact priority values are not defined by the case.
- Priority values must be agreed upon before implementation.

### Trade Offer Creation

- Members may submit offers for unfulfilled wishlist items.
- The offered game is the game referenced by the wishlist item.
- The offer creator specifies which catalogue game they want in return.
- A new offer receives status `OPEN`.
- The creation date must be recorded.
- The system does not verify ownership of the offered game.

### Accepting Offers

- Only the wishlist owner can accept an offer.
- The offer must be open and not expired.
- The associated wishlist item must not already be fulfilled.
- Acceptance changes the offer status to `ACCEPTED`.
- Acceptance marks the wishlist item as fulfilled.
- Conflicting open offers must be cancelled automatically.

### Rejecting Offers

- Only the wishlist owner can reject an offer.
- Rejection changes the offer status to `REJECTED`.
- Rejection does not fulfill the wishlist item.
- Rejection does not automatically cancel unrelated offers.

### Cancelling Offers

- Only the offer creator can manually cancel their offer.
- Manual cancellation is only permitted while the offer is open.
- Accepted, rejected and cancelled offers cannot be manually cancelled again.
- The system may automatically cancel conflicting open offers after another offer is accepted.

### Offer Expiration

- Every offer has a limited validity period.
- The validity period is calculated from the creation date.
- The system automatically determines whether the offer has expired.
- An expired offer cannot be accepted.
- Expiration does not require a manually assigned status.
- The validity period must be configured according to the club's rules.

### Fulfilled Wishlist Items

- A wishlist item becomes fulfilled when an offer is accepted.
- A fulfilled wishlist item cannot receive new trade offers.
- The fulfilled status is stored with the wishlist item.
- The case does not specify a manual reopening action.

### Conflicting Trade Offers

- A member may offer the same game to multiple other members at the same time.
- When one of those offers is accepted, other open offers involving the same offer creator and offered game must be cancelled.
- Cancellation applies to matching offers even when they belong to different wishlist owners.
- Unrelated offers must remain unchanged.
- The acceptance and conflicting-offer cancellation should be handled as one atomic backend operation.

### Ownership Verification

- The system does not check whether the offer creator actually owns the offered game.
- A game does not need to appear in the offer creator's personal collection.
- The club relies on trust between members.
- Trade offers must not be rejected solely because the offered game is absent from the member's collection.

### Physical Exchange

- Trading involves exchanging one game for another.
- No prices or monetary transactions are involved.
- Games are exchanged in person.
- The case does not require shipping or payment functionality.

## Example Invalid Actions

The system must reject invalid actions.

Examples:

1. **Accepting another member's offer:**  
   A member tries to accept an offer associated with a wishlist item they do not own.

   **Expected result:** The backend rejects the action as forbidden. The offer remains unchanged.

2. **Rejecting another member's offer:**  
   A member tries to reject an offer belonging to another member's wishlist item.

   **Expected result:** The system rejects the action because only the wishlist owner can reject the offer.

3. **Cancelling another member's offer:**  
   A member tries to cancel an offer created by someone else.

   **Expected result:** The backend rejects the action as forbidden.

4. **Cancelling an accepted offer:**  
   An offer creator tries to cancel an offer that has already been accepted.

   **Expected result:** The system rejects the action because cancellation is only allowed while the offer is open.

5. **Accepting an expired offer:**  
   A wishlist owner tries to accept an offer after its validity period has passed.

   **Expected result:** The system rejects the action and explains that the offer has expired.

6. **Offering a game for a fulfilled wishlist item:**  
   A member tries to create a trade offer for a wishlist item marked `isFulfilled = true`.

   **Expected result:** The system rejects the action and does not create a new offer.

7. **Accepting an already rejected offer:**  
   A wishlist owner tries to accept an offer with status `REJECTED`.

   **Expected result:** The system rejects the action because the offer is no longer open.

8. **Accepting a cancelled offer:**  
   A wishlist owner tries to accept an offer with status `CANCELLED`.

   **Expected result:** The system rejects the action because cancelled offers cannot be accepted.

9. **Accepting a second conflicting offer:**  
   A member offers the same game to two different wishlist owners. The first offer is accepted. Another wishlist owner then tries to accept the second offer.

   **Expected result:** The second offer has already been automatically cancelled and cannot be accepted.

10. **Modifying another member's wishlist:**  
    A member attempts to modify a wishlist item belonging to another member.

    **Expected result:** The system rejects the action as forbidden.

11. **Concurrent conflicting acceptances:**  
    Two wishlist owners attempt to accept offers involving the same offer creator and offered game at nearly the same time.

    **Expected result:** Only one conflicting offer may be accepted. The other must be cancelled or rejected as a conflict without producing inconsistent data.

## Open Decisions

The following details are not explicitly defined in the GameShelf case and should be confirmed with the product owner or project group before implementation:

- **Priority values:** Should priorities use `LOW`, `MEDIUM` and `HIGH`, numeric values, or another system?
- **Offer validity period:** How long does a trade offer remain valid?
- **Editing wishlist items:** Can members change the priority or notes after creating an item?
- **Removing wishlist items:** Can members delete wishlist items, and what happens to associated open offers?
- **Duplicate wishlist items:** Can a member add the same catalogue game more than once?
- **Own wishlist offers:** Should members be prevented from making offers on their own wishlist items?
- **Expired-offer cancellation:** Can the offer creator manually cancel an expired offer that still has status `OPEN`?
- **Fulfilled-item offers:** What should happen to other open offers on the same fulfilled wishlist item if they do not match the specified conflicting-offer rule?
- **Reopening fulfilled items:** Can a fulfilled wishlist item ever become unfulfilled again?
- **Physical trade completion:** Is accepting an offer sufficient to complete the system workflow, or should physical handover be recorded separately?
- **Offer notifications:** Should members receive notifications when offers are created, accepted, rejected or cancelled?
- **Trade history:** Should completed and cancelled offers remain visible indefinitely?

These decisions should be resolved before implementing functionality that depends on them.
